# The test targets and benches the Nightly's Mutants shards leave out of the
# cargo oracle (#310, #401), one `<kind> <name>` a line, kind `test` (under
# tests/) or `bench` (under benches/). Each runs no line of a floored file
# (the files of MUTANTS_FLOORS in .github/workflows/nightly.yml), measured
# with cargo llvm-cov per target, so it cannot change a floored file's
# verdict. The selection step and the guard both read this file and nothing
# else: .github/nightly/no_floored.py measures each entry's reach and fails
# naming the entry and the floored line it runs, and its record
# .github/nightly/no-floored-reach.json is checked against this list by CI's
# ratchet job (docs/NIGHTLY.md).
#
# The eight architecture scanners and rule 28's sites read the source as text.
test arch_config_env
test arch_env_reads
test arch_explorer_sites
test arch_no_error_words
test arch_no_prefix_errors
test arch_no_unwrap
test arch_spawn_sites
test arch_sql_sites
test rule_28_sites
# The BRC-100 oracle reads the committed fixtures.
test brc100
# Other modules only.
test header_source
test signing_digest_vector
# internalize_action runs server/post_word.rs alone; list_outputs no line of
# src/ (cd53740).
bench internalize_action
bench list_outputs
